       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4250 mg PO TID, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum:** the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Your order is about 5 times that.\n- **Risk:** a dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg PO TID with meals**, if the extra \"0\" was a typo for a lower dose\n- **500 mg PO TID or 1,000 mg PO BID**, or another regimen\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is what you want, please confirm that and give me a reason to add to the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
